---
import ContentPage from "../components/ContentPage.astro";
---

<ContentPage
	title="About | PAN Card Photo Resizer Online"
	description="Learn about NSDL Photo Resize, an independent online tool to crop and resize PAN card photos and signatures privately in your browser."
	canonicalUrl="https://nsdlphotoresize.com/about/"
	eyebrow="About this tool"
	heading="A simpler way to prepare PAN application images"
	intro="NSDL Photo Resize is an independent browser-based utility for preparing photo and signature files for PAN application uploads. Crop an image, adjust its dimensions, and save a JPEG without installing editing software."
>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">What the PAN photo resizer does</h2>
		<p>
			This PAN card photo resizer helps you prepare a photograph or
			signature image with adjustable width, height, and resolution. It
			includes practical presets for common image types, an interactive
			crop preview, and portal-specific JPEG size limits. Choose the
			NSDL/Protean or UTIITSL preset to load its photo or signature
			dimensions, resolution, and file-size limit. You can use the same
			tool whether you searched for an NSDL photo resize, a UTI photo
			resize, or a PAN card signature resizer.
		</p>
		<p>
			Select a JPG, PNG, or WebP from your device, adjust the crop, review
			the output, and download the result. The image is processed in your
			browser; it is not uploaded to this website, and your original file
			is left unchanged.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Independent and privacy-conscious</h2>
		<p>
			This site is not affiliated with or endorsed by Protean, NSDL, or
			UTIITSL. Names of application services are used only to describe
			where applicants may need image files. Portal rules can change or
			vary by application type, so confirm the latest dimensions, file
			format, resolution, and size limits on the official portal before
			uploading.
		</p>
		<p>
			The tool prepares image files only. It does not submit a PAN
			application, store documents, validate personal details, or
			guarantee that an image or application will be accepted.
		</p>
	</section>
	<p>
		<a class="text-link" href="/features/">Explore the image resizer features</a>
		<span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
		<a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works/">See how it works</a>
	</p>
</ContentPage>
